#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A or B is yes. C or D is no."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A sibling that owns a PR in the batch names the head it wants merged."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Broadcast the hold to siblings"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Called by the merge manager watch when queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or when the owner says the runners are full."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Cancel queued PR runs; build, push, merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:69
#. Diagram label
msgid "Choose A, B, C or D"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Dry-run, then ask the owner naming every PR"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:22
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every other session with a PR in the queue. It acts once: it stops pushing when the hold arrives and names the head it wants merged, so the steward stacks a branch nobody is still moving. It does not choose what lands; the owner does."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Go?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hold released, nothing merged"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hold, and name the heads to merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Landed and reported"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Landing a batch while the runners are full: cancel everything queued, pause new work, consolidate all ready PRs on one meta-merge branch, skip CI and rendering, and merge it, holding the swarm siblings until it is done. It repeats across repositories. Skill saturation-meta-merge holds the steps, the safety rules and the record of its first run. This process bypasses merge:guard on purpose, so the owner's card, the PR body and a comment on each member PR are the record."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:25
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:94
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merged?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Message every sibling that pushes to the repositories involved: what is about to land, and hold pushes, merges and run cancels until done. Ask the coordinator to pass it on to any thread that cannot be reached."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Never cancel a main push run that has started. Build from fresh main with merge commits, skipping conflicts, .github/workflows/ and subscriptions/. Open one PR per repository, merge it with a merge commit, and comment on each member PR with the link."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:106
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One message to the owner: what merged, main's verdict per repository, and any open decision. On red, the fix goes to main as its own PR."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:70
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only the owner's own tap or words approve the landing. A PR the card does not name gets no merge from it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "Post done to every held sibling"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:88
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Post done with what landed and what is still open, also when nothing was merged. A hold with no done is an outage."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:105
#. Diagram label
msgid "Report what landed and main's verdict"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run main's checks"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Runners saturated"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:16
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge: land the ready PRs when the runners are full"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:21
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sibling session"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stack the PRs on a meta-merge branch without pushing. Then post the full question (include, leave out with the reason, merge method, per repository), followed by the card: A go, B also the red ones, C dry run only, D cancel."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The CI system, which runs main's checks once on the merged result. Its verdict is what the steward reports; it is drawn as its own lane because it is a system acting on a fixed program, not a choice anybody makes."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager, acting as merge steward for the duration of the drain. It notices the runners are saturated, holds the swarm, dry-runs the meta-merge and asks the owner with every PR named; on a yes it cancels the queued PR runs, builds and lands the meta-merge branch, releases the hold and reports. It never lands anything the owner's card did not name."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge starts main's checks. Until tools#1384, a closed PR's run can cancel them, so the steward re-runs a cancelled main run."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The repository owner, the only lane that decides. A meta-merge lands PRs on main without their own CI, so the choice between the offered options is a person's, made on a card that names each PR; a PR the card does not name gets no merge."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:122
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""
